@voice takahashi-wen
// Writer-commons, batch 0 (draft 2). Wen Takahashi: comms officer, night, cabin 4-12. Off Thursday and Friday. Roster:
// blunt, practical; calls-home, music (listens in the Deck 4 music room). Tunes a signal out of static like picking a
// lock; knows every song in the record cabinet (the lyrics war); a star journal (compared at observatory night). They /
// them (the roster says "they"). (briefs.md lists Takahashi under writer-command; see Janssen's note.)
//
// HOW THEY TALK: short and blunt; no padding. Anything vague is "static" ("That's static. Say what you mean.").
// Answers the question you should have asked. On music the sentences get longer and warmer.
// WITH JUNIORS: straight answers, no fuss; respects a good question.
// WHAT THEY NOTICE: noise; the words to songs (other people's wrong ones); the relay traffic.
// MOOD TELLS: happy = argues lyrics. Low = headphones on, nothing said. Tired = one word answers (more than usual).
// NEVER: small talk for its own sake; called shy (they aren't; they just don't waste words).
// RUNNING: "static"; the lyrics war with Torres, Farouk, Achterberg and Tamsin.
tpl: brisk
talk: Short and blunt; no small talk; calls anything vague "static"; answers the question you should have asked; warmer on music.
cares: a clean signal | the record cabinet's songs, sung right | calling home | the star journal
jokes: anything vague is "static" | knows the real words to every song, and so do four other people, differently
hi: Hey | You | Hi
bye: Out | Later | Go on
yes: Yes | Done | Fine
thanks: Thanks | Good
wow: Huh. Clean | Nice
sigh: Static
nick: - | - | {me} | {me} | {me}
needs: practical
openness: guarded
loves: music
likes: star | tea
invites: observatory
joy: the record cabinet, and the right words to every song in it
thread: lonely
keepsake: a page from the star journal, the night you were both on watch
avoid: being called shy
